=============================
Q) git merge vs git rebase
==========================

git merge:

=> Combines changes from one branch into another branch.

Example:

```
    git switch develop

    git merge feature/login
```

Merge creates a merge commit when required by the repository
history/configuration.

git rebase:

=> Replays commits from one branch on top of another base.

Example:

```
    git switch feature/login

    git rebase develop
```

Benefits:

```
    Cleaner linear history in suitable workflows
```

Important:

Do not rebase shared/public branches casually.

Rebase rewrites commit history.

If commits have already been pushed and shared with other
developers, coordinate with the team before rewriting history.

