GitHub Authentication
=====================

=> GitHub repositories can be accessed using secure authentication
methods.

Common methods:

```
    1) SSH authentication

    2) Personal Access Token

    3) GitHub CLI authentication
```

For DevOps/Linux servers, SSH authentication is commonly used.

# Generate SSH key

ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "[your-email@example.com](mailto:your-email@example.com)"

# Start SSH agent

eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"

# Add private key to SSH agent

ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

# Display public key

cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

=> Copy the public key and add it to GitHub:

```
    GitHub
       |
       v
    Settings
       |
       v
    SSH and GPG keys
       |
       v
    New SSH key
```

# Test GitHub SSH connection

ssh -T [git@github.com](mailto:git@github.com)

Then clone using SSH:

git clone [git@github.com](mailto:git@github.com):<username>/<repository>.git

IMPORTANT:

Never share:

```
    ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
```

The private key must remain private.

Only the public key:

```
    ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

should be added to GitHub.

