==========================
Git Reset
=========

=> `git reset` can move the current branch reference and,
depending on the option, modify staging/working tree.

# Soft reset

git reset --soft HEAD~1

=> Commit is removed from branch history,
but changes remain staged.

# Mixed reset

git reset HEAD~1

=> Commit is removed from branch history,
changes remain in working tree.

# Hard reset

git reset --hard HEAD~1

=> Commit and changes can be removed.

WARNING:

`git reset --hard` can permanently discard uncommitted work.

Use carefully.

