==========================
Git Cherry-Pick
===============

=> `git cherry-pick` applies the changes introduced by
a specific commit onto the current branch.

Example:

```
    git switch release

    git cherry-pick <commit-id>
```

Real-time usecase:

A production hotfix was implemented in another branch.

Instead of merging the complete branch, the team may decide
to bring only the required hotfix commit.

Note:

Cherry-pick can create conflicts.

After resolving:

```
    git add .

    git cherry-pick --continue
```

To cancel cherry-pick:

```
    git cherry-pick --abort
```

