=========================
Production Git Guidelines
=========================

1. Never commit passwords.

2. Never commit API keys.

3. Never commit AWS credentials.

4. Never commit private SSH keys.

5. Never force-push shared branches unless explicitly approved.

6. Protect important branches.

7. Use Pull Requests for code review.

8. Use CI checks before merge.

9. Use meaningful commit messages.

10. Keep commits focused.

11. Pull/fetch latest changes before starting work.

12. Do not use `git reset --hard` without understanding
    what will be deleted.

13. Do not use `git clean -fd` without checking the preview.

14. Tag production releases.

15. Keep production deployment traceable to a Git commit/tag.

